<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kazys Škirpa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1895–1979</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kazys Škirpa was a Lithuanian army officer and diplomat, envoy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuanian-activist-front">Lithuanian Activist Front</a> there in 1940 after the Soviet occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>. He was named prime minister of the provisional government proclaimed during the June Uprising of 1941, but the Germans kept him under house arrest in Berlin. He later emigrated to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kazys-skirpa.jpg" alt="Kazys Škirpa" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kazys_Skirpa.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
